20260517132706 [ignoring loop detection] Here is a summary of the root causes and the elegant solution that has been implemented to solve the subtitle-only viewing experience: 🔍 Root Cause Analysis The $0.00$ Pause Gap (Context Missing): When opening a virtual color canvas (av://lavfi:...) without standard video tracks, the timeline defaults to pausing at exactly 0.00 seconds. However, subtitle tracks (even corrupt or poorly formatted auto-subtitle streams) almost never contain subtitle entries beginning at exactly 00:00:00,000. Because of this, no active subtitle card was selected on launch. Since no subtitle card was active, Kardenwort initialized with an active index of -1 (meaning no active word selection, no multi-line scroll focus, and no active subtitle context). This caused the Kardenwort overlay to be completely hidden, which made the keys feel unresponsive and caused the player to fall back to mpv's default global playback keys instead of Kardenwort's custom interactive binding matrix. Selecting Multiple Files Clash: When selecting both subtitle files in Windows Explorer and sending them via the "Send to" shortcut, Windows Explorer spawned two parallel processes of viewer.py at the exact same moment. They both searched the directory, located each other, and launched separate conflicting instances of mpv simultaneously, causing the launcher processes to clash and block the window from displaying. 🛠️ The Solution Auto-Seeking to the First Subtitle on Load: I upgraded viewer.py with a robust subtitle parser function (get_first_sub_start). It scans the primary subtitle file (fully supporting.srt,.vtt, and.ass formatting) and automatically finds the timestamp of the first valid subtitle entry (gracefully skipping corrupt or negative offset entries). We then pass this timestamp as the --start= option directly to mpv! Now, the player instantly starts at the exact millisecond of the first subtitle card. The primary and secondary subtitle tracks are rendered immediately by the Kardenwort OSD on load. Since an active subtitle card is immediately in focus, the entire Kardenwort keybinding matrix (like smart-space, s for replay, a/d for seeking, and z for the Drum Window) is immediately active, fully loaded, and ready to use! Single-Selection Subtitle Auto-Linking: The launcher script already contains logic to automatically search the folder and load the secondary translation track (e.g. matching.ru.srt next to.en.srt) and link the highlight database.tsv file automatically. You only need to select and send the primary subtitle track (e.g. *.en.srt), and the launcher script will automatically handle the secondary track and database configuration, loading both perfectly in a single clean player window!
