20260517133248 Thank you so much for the screenshots! They are incredibly helpful and show exactly what went wrong: 🔍 The Bug Explained In the screenshot, the error message reads: FileNotFoundError: Subtitle file not found: C:\Users\voothi\Documents\...\20260517131337\%1 Why? When creating the shortcut via WScript Shell, the installer explicitly passed "%1" inside the.lnk file arguments. However, in Windows "Send to" shortcuts, Windows Explorer does not automatically replace %1 with the file path. Instead, it literally passes "%1" as the first argument, and then appends the actual subtitle file path as the second argument! This caused sys.argv[1] to literalize as "%1". When the script tried to load that path, it failed and popped up the error box. 🛠️ The Fix I have applied a dual-defense fix to resolve this perfectly: Defensive Argument Fallback: I updated viewer.py to gracefully detect if Windows Explorer passes "%1" literally as the first argument. If it does, the script automatically ignores it and falls back to using the second argument (sys.argv[2]), which is the real, actual subtitle file path. This ensures the viewer works perfectly even with old, unchanged shortcuts! Clean Arguments Re-creation: I modified install.py to remove the useless literal "%1" from the shortcut arguments, and automatically ran the installer to rebuild a perfectly formatted, clean shortcut in your SendTo directory. 🎉 Test It Now! The installer has run successfully, and the script handles the literal argument perfectly. Simply right-click a single subtitle file (e.g. *.en.srt), and click Send to -> Kardenwort Sub Viewer. It will open instantly with a black background, auto-seek directly to the first subtitle card, load the matching translation track (e.g. *.ru.srt), and initialize the interactive Kardenwort UI immediately!
