20260521103401 # Why if I turn off subtitles with the c key, then press z to go to DW, in this mode the e tooltip does not work for me, X appears instead, and only works if the subtitles are turned on? ## Description Also f, g, h, combinations with Shift, in EN/RU do not work. Also check out related options that I may have missed. [[20260519123326-почему-если-я-отключаю|Почему если я отключаю субтитры клавишей c, дальше нажимаю z для перехода в DW, в этом режиме у меня не работает по клавише e tooltip, вместо него появляется X, а работает только если субтитры включены?]] 20260521103446 # Shift+q does not work with Secondary Sub OFF. ## Description [[20260520152915-shiftq-не-работает-при|Shift+q не работает при Secondary Sub OFF.]]
20260521104040 Here is the explanation and details of the changes implemented in the codebase to resolve these issues. 1. Tooltip (e / У), f, g, and h keys showing "X" when Subtitles are OFF The Cause When subtitles are toggled OFF via the c key (Cyrillic с), the state variable FSM.native_sub_vis is set to false. Inside the Drum Window (DW, toggled via z / я), interactive functions (such as tooltip toggle e, pink pairing f, smart-add to Anki g, toggle-anki-global h, and search) check if subtitles are visible via if not FSM.native_sub_vis then show_osd("X") return end. Because FSM.native_sub_vis is false, pressing these keys in DW triggered the visibility guard, displayed X, and aborted. The Solution We updated scripts/kardenwort/main.lua to make these visibility guards DW-aware. They now check: lua if not FSM.native_sub_vis and FSM.DRUM_WINDOW == "OFF" then show_osd("X") return end This permits interactive keys (e, f, g, h, search, copy, etc.) to function normally inside the Drum Window even when master subtitle visibility is turned off via c. 2. Shift+q (Q / Й) Not Working with Secondary Sub OFF The Cause When the secondary translation track is turned off (Secondary Sub OFF), FSM.MEDIA_STATE is set to "SINGLE_SRT". The cmd_cycle_copy_mode() function had a guard block: lua if FSM.MEDIA_STATE == "SINGLE_SRT" then show_osd("Copy Mode: Fixed to Primary (Single Track)") return end This immediately blocked copying translation text even if secondary subtitles were preloaded in cache. The Solution We modified the logic in cmd_cycle_copy_mode() to check if secondary track subtitle cache FSM.DW_TOOLTIP_SEC_SUBS is available: lua local has_sec = (Tracks.sec.id ~= 0 and Tracks.sec.subs and #Tracks.sec.subs > 0) or (FSM.DW_TOOLTIP_SEC_SUBS and #FSM.DW_TOOLTIP_SEC_SUBS > 0) if not has_sec then show_osd("Copy Mode: Fixed to Primary (Single Track)") return end We also updated prepare_export_text in main.lua to successfully fall back to FSM.DW_TOOLTIP_SEC_SUBS when Copy Mode: B (translation) is selected. You can now cycle copy modes and copy translation text even with the secondary track visually turned off. 3. Explanation of Shift+f, Shift+g, and Shift+h behavior Shift+f (F / А - Cycle Immersion Mode) Behavior: This hotkey does not have a subtitle visibility guard. It cycles immersion mode between PHRASE and MOVIE globally. DW Behavior: Inside the Drum Window, standard video playback boundaries are not processed because DW is a static scrollable view. Therefore, changing immersion mode has no visual impact inside DW itself. Shift+g (G / П) Behavior: This key is mapped to ignore in input.conf by design and has no registered function. Shift+h (H / Р - Toggle Karaoke Mode) Behavior: This toggles the pause granularity (every word vs. end of phrase). Guards: It is heavily restricted by design: if FSM.DRUM_WINDOW ~= "OFF" -> Explicitly blocked inside the Drum Window, printing X. if not FSM.MEDIA_STATE:match("ASS") -> Blocked on non-ASS tracks (like SRT, or if no track format matches), printing X.
20260521104712 When the second subtitle is disabled, Shift+c in DW (z) mode does not work in Subtitle Mode B, the Context Mode ON function does not work (it works like OFF)
20260521105222 Bug Analysis & Root Cause The issue occurs when copying subtitles in the Drum Window (z mode) via Shift+C (dictionary lookup copy / key_copy_popup) when the secondary translation subtitle track is visually turned off (Secondary Sub OFF / secondary-sid set to 0). Context Harvesting: In this state, get_clipboard_text_smart() invokes get_copy_context_text() to collect the context paragraphs. Context Resolution: The internal helper append() was hard-restricted to search only files at Tracks.pri.path and Tracks.sec.path. Behavior in Mode B: Since Tracks.sec.path is nil or empty when secondary subs are disabled, the append routine failed to extract the Russian (Cyrillic) translation sentences under Subtitle Mode B (which filters out English and keeps Russian). Failure to Return Context: Consequently, get_copy_context_text() returned nothing for the translation context. The copy command fell back to regular single-line copy, behaving exactly as if Context Mode was OFF. Implemented Solution We updated the subtitle extraction pipeline in scripts/kardenwort/main.lua to leverage the preloaded translation cache (FSM.DW_TOOLTIP_SEC_SUBS), which is automatically populated by the suite's automatic probing mechanism when secondary subtitles are disabled: Generalizing Context Appending: We refactored append() inside get_copy_context_text to accept a provided_subs table directly: lua local function append(path, is_ass, explicit_idx, provided_subs) if not path and not provided_subs then return end local subs = provided_subs if not subs then if Tracks.pri.path == path and FSM.DRUM == "ON" and not is_ass then subs = Tracks.pri.subs elseif Tracks.sec.path == path and FSM.DRUM == "ON" and not is_ass then subs = Tracks.sec.subs else subs = load_sub(path, is_ass) end end -... normal context building logic follows... Adding the Cache Fallback: We added a fallback route to load translation context directly from FSM.DW_TOOLTIP_SEC_SUBS when Tracks.sec.path is unavailable: lua append(Tracks.pri.path, Tracks.pri.is_ass, line_idx) if Tracks.sec.path and Tracks.sec.path ~= Tracks.pri.path then append(Tracks.sec.path, Tracks.sec.is_ass) elseif FSM.DW_TOOLTIP_SEC_SUBS and #FSM.DW_TOOLTIP_SEC_SUBS > 0 then append(nil, false, nil, FSM.DW_TOOLTIP_SEC_SUBS) end Verification and Test Suite Results To ensure this behavior behaves correctly, we added a dedicated acceptance test test_20260521104712_dw_copy_context_mode_b_fallback to tests/acceptance/test_20260427003254_copy_sub_fallback.py. The tests have been verified: Newly Added Acceptance Test: pytest tests/acceptance/test_20260427003254_copy_sub_fallback.py -k test_20260521104712_dw_copy_context_mode_b_fallback -> PASSED Other Regression Suite Checks: All related tests in the copy fallback suite pass cleanly.
