20260521154447 x x x x All 5 tests still pass with wrap_mul = 1.05 applied across all three layout sites. Summary Problem: Wrapped lines within a single subtitle use vline_h = font_size × 0.87, which is tighter than the font's natural line height (~1.0) — descenders on letters like g, j, y collide with the next visual line. The same 0.87 is also baked into the inter-subtitle gap formula, so bumping dw_line_height_mul globally would over-space subtitles too. Fix — decouple intra-subtitle wrap spacing from inter-subtitle spacing: SiteChange Options table:353New dw_wrap_line_height_mul = 1.05 dw_build_layout:4048vline_h uses wrap_mul (falls back to lh_mul) draw_dw:4270Same — keeps hit-zone geometry aligned with render ensure_sub_layout:6306Same — keeps cached entry.height aligned calculate_sub_gap is untouched, so inter-subtitle gap retains its existing calibration (lh_mul=0.87 + block_gap_mul=-0.27). Net effect at default dw_font_size=34: visual line height grows from 29.6 → 35.7 px (+6 px) — enough vertical clearance for descenders without disturbing inter-subtitle spacing. If 1.05 still feels tight, try 1.10 in your script-opts. If too loose, drop to 1.0.
