20260521155242 x x x x Summary Problem: In DM mode, you can't click punctuation (.,?,!) to select it. In DW mode you can. Root cause: main.lua:3775 in calculate_osd_line_meta (called by draw_drum) filters tokens with if t.is_word and t.logical_idx. The tokenizer (main.lua:1742-1756) assigns integer logical_idx to words and fractional logical_idx to punctuation — but the DM filter also requires is_word=true, so punctuation never enters line.words. drum_osd_hit_test can only return what's in line.words, so the period/question mark is unreachable. DW's parallel path (draw_dw:4283) uses only if t.logical_idx and includes punctuation correctly. Fix: One-character change — drop the t.is_word and guard in DM to match DW. Punctuation tokens flow into line.words with their fractional logical_idx; the closest-center loop in drum_osd_hit_test picks them up like any other word; downstream selection / highlight code already handles fractional logical_idx (proven by DW). Validation: All 4 existing DM-touching acceptance tests still pass (test_20260512095351_dm_selection_geometry_stability.py, test_20260511100252_rmb_gap_parity.py). Manual verification: clicking a trailing. or? in DM should now select it and let you press the highlight key to turn it yellow, same as DW. Want me to add a focused regression test (clicks the? in a known fixture subtitle in DM and asserts the returned logical_idx is fractional), or wait for your manual verification first?
