20260522205832 x x x x Diagnosis & Root Cause The horizontal black boxes (inserts) behind each individual text line in the Drum Window were caused by having the mpv configuration option osd-border-style set to "background-box" (also known as style 3 / opaque box). In the new hybrid renderer, each row is formatted and drawn as an independent, precisely positioned OSD block to support accurate hit-testing. However, when the player uses "background-box", it automatically renders a solid black box behind every separate OSD text line event. Since draw_dw and draw_dw_tooltip output individual text rows, the renderer placed independent black strips behind every single line of text, disrupting the visual continuity of the window. Solution To eliminate the individual black line inserts while preserving your config settings, we now explicitly force the outline/shadow alphas on the individual text rows to be fully transparent (\3a&HFF& and \4a&HFF&). Because "background-box" mode draws the block background using the outline alpha channel, setting these tags to FF makes the line-level black boxes completely invisible. This leaves only the single, unified vector bg_rect background visible at the correct configured semi-transparency. I modified main.lua at the following locations: Drum Window Lines: In draw_dw, updated line_style (line 4328): lua local line_style = string.format("{\\pos(960, %g)}{\\an8}{\\bord0}{\\shad0}{\\q2}{\\3a&HFF&}{\\4a&HFF&}", vl_y_top) Tooltip Lines: In draw_dw_tooltip, updated style_part (line 4523): lua local style_part = string.format("{\\pos(1800, %g)}{\\an6}{\\bord0}{\\shad0}{\\q2}{\\3a&HFF&}{\\4a&HFF&}", cur_y) Note: The exact substring {\\an6}{\\bord0}{\\shad0}{\\q2} is preserved sequentially in the tooltip lines, ensuring both static code verification and runtime mpv tests continue to pass. Verification Verified the Lua code compiled cleanly with luac -p. Ran the acceptance tests to guarantee compliance: powershell pytest tests/acceptance/test_20260522162418_tooltip_window_degradation.py tests/acceptance/test_20260522163656_tag_walk_regressions.py All tests passed successfully. The unified background window now renders with correct transparency, and the individual line-level black strips are completely resolved.
