20260523134531 x x x x x Done. Both tooltip issues addressed. Issue 1 — text extends beyond the semi-transparent rectangle (docs/assets/20260523132907.png) Root cause: dw_get_str_width's proportional-font heuristic at main.lua:3772 used fs * 0.45 for Cyrillic glyphs; Inter renders Cyrillic at ~0.50-0.55, so long Russian lines were ~10% wider than computed. min_x = math.min(min_x, 1800 - vl.width) ended up too far right, leaving text poking out the left of the \p1 rect. Fix: bumped to fs * 0.52 with explanatory comment. Issue 2 — tooltip darker in DM (drum) mode (docs/assets/20260523132926.png) Root cause: when osd-border-style = "background-box", mpv draws its own background-box for every \pos text line. The tooltip additionally draws a shared \p1 vector card — result is a double-dark stack. DW already solved this by routing open/close through manage_ui_border_override (which temporarily switches osd-border-style to outline-and-shadow). The tooltip code didn't. Fix: forward-declared manage_ui_border_override, added an apply_tooltip_ass(ass) helper at main.lua:3022 that engages/releases the override on visibility transitions, and routed all 8 dw_tooltip_osd.data =... writes through the helper (clear_tooltip_overlay, flush_rendering_caches, cmd_dw_tooltip_pin, cmd_dw_tooltip_toggle, dw_tooltip_mouse_update x2, make_mouse_handler dismiss path, test-tooltip-pin script message). Tests added (5) test_dw_pure_logic.py: 3 Python ports — Cyrillic constant lower bound, drift comparison vs old value, ASCII unchanged. tag_walk_regressions.py: test_tooltip_visibility_engages_ui_border_override, test_manage_ui_border_override_is_forward_declared, test_dw_get_str_width_cyrillic_estimate_at_least_052. Test results Impacted suites (tests/unit/test_dw_pure_logic.py + tag_walk_regressions + tooltip_window_degradation + spec_depth_pass2) → 101 passed in 30.7s — the spec_depth suite boots mpv, confirming the script still loads cleanly. Foundation IPC suite → 5 passed in 14.9s — confirms