istered. Viewed main.lua:7120-7220 20260524105616 I will read lines 7220 to 7320 of `main.lua` to see the registration logic and loops inside `manage_dw_bindings`. Viewed main.lua:7220-7320 20260524105616 I will search for `DW_MOUSE_DRAGGING` and related dragging functions to locate where the mouse dragging loop and mouse scroll timer are handled. Ran command: `Select-String -Path "U:\voothi\20260308110646-kardenwort-mpv\scripts\kardenwort\main.lua" -Pattern "DW_MOUSE_DRAGGING"` 20260524105616 I will read lines 5460 to 5520 of `main.lua` to see how the mouse click and dragging callbacks are registered and processed. Viewed main.lua:5460-5520 20260524105616 I will read lines 5410 to 5460 of `main.lua` to see the initial mouse coordinate capture on mouse down. Viewed main.lua:5410-5460 20260524105616 I will search for `dw_mouse_update_selection` in `main.lua` to see how dragging updates are handled. Ran command: `Select-String -Path "U:\voothi\20260308110646-kardenwort-mpv\scripts\kardenwort\main.lua" -Pattern "function dw_mouse_update_selection"` 20260524105616 I will read lines 4830 to 4890 of `main.lua` to see the dragging selection update logic. Viewed main.lua:4830-4890 20260524105616 I will read lines 5520 to 5560 of `main.lua` to see the end of the mouse `up` event handler. Viewed main.lua:5520-5560 20260524105616 I will apply all Phase 4 changes, introducing the drag threshold check to filter minor cursor noise and rewriting the dynamic keybinding loop with explicit callback safety. Edited main.lua 20260524105616 I will update the `task.md` checklist to mark Phase 4 as completed. Edited task.md 20260524105616 I will write the `walkthrough.md` artifact to present our achievements, implementation details, and step-by-step progress to the user for review. Edited walkthrough.md 20260524105616 I will update the `task.md` checklist to mark the verification status. Edited task.md 20260524105616 I have completed the implementation of the approved plan. Below is a summary of the changes introduced to resolve the spacing, alignment, mouse hit-testing drift, and sub-box transparency conflicts under the global `osd-border-style=background-box` configuration: ### 1. Spacing and Margin Offsets (Phase 1) - Delegated Cyrillic proportional width scaling to `DW_HELPERS.dw_get_str_width_proportional()` with the calibrated `0.52 * fs` scale factor to prevent trailing character truncation. - Decoupled subtitle-level block gaps from visual wrapped line heights via `DW_HELPERS.vline_height()`. - Clamped viewports within the defined edge margin boundaries using `DW_HELPERS.calculate_block_top()`. - Exposed visual offsets (`dw_block_top`, `dw_total_height`) in OSD query state snapshots. ### 2. Render-Cached Mouse Hit-Testing (Phase 2) - Added dynamic, absolute hit-zones (`FSM.DW_HIT_ZONES`) that populate in sync with the visual rendering pass. - Cached these zones in `DW_DRAW_CACHE.hit_zones` to avoid CPU recalculation. - Rewrote `dw_hit_test()` to query the cached rendering coordinates directly, eliminating layout/spacing estimation drift and supporting snaps. - Removed the restrictive `is_word` filter in visual line metadata to allow punctuation and special character selections in DM mode. ### 3. Cohesive Background and Localized OSD Transparency (Phase 3) - Rendered a single cohesive vector background card (`bg_rect` via `\p1`) matching the visual text block geometry. - Laid out and drew each visual line as an independent OSD event using absolute vertical and horizontal coordinates. - Neutralized individual box layers under `osd-border-style=background-box` by prepending `\3a&HFF&\4a&HFF&\bord0\shad0` to OSD events and highlighted words, eliminating layered box conflicts. ### 4. Drag Thresholds and Binding Loops (Phase 4) - Deferred mouse scroll timers and active drag states until a `5px` movement threshold is exceeded. - Refactored `manage_dw_bindings()` dynamic key/mouse registration into a clean, table-driven loop checking `type(cb) == "function"`, guaranteeing stability against malformed options. --### Artifacts Created - [walkthrough.md](file:///C:/Users/voothi/.gemini/antigravity-ide/brain/4aeda6c0-19d2-44d2-9cce-2a9bc9956b4d/walkthrough.md): Detailed architectural overview and manual verification steps. - [task.md](file:///C:/Users/voothi/.gemini/antigravity-ide/brain/4aeda6c0-19d2-44d2-9cce-2a9bc9956b4d/task.md): Progress checklist tracking. Please review the visual presentation on your system under the `outline-and-shadow` and `background-box` styles. Once you verify that the visual prototype renders correctly, we can proceed to migrate the old tests and execute the automated verification suite.
