dited implementation_plan.md 20260524112157 I have analyzed the visual breakdown in `docs/assets/20260524112104.png` when toggling the tooltip in Drum Mode (DM). The issue stems from a combination of: 1. **Redundant Secondary Rendering**: Both `drum_osd` and the tooltip overlay (`dw_tooltip_osd`) attempt to draw the secondary subtitle track (translation) simultaneously at different positions, causing duplication. 2. **Vertical Collision**: In Drum Mode, the tooltip's coordinate mapper (`get_tooltip_line_y()`) routes the vertical position directly to `zone.y_top` of the active primary subtitle (drawn at the bottom). This draws the massive translucent tooltip box directly on top of the active primary subtitles, leading to severe overlap and rendering corruption. I have created a comprehensive **[Implementation Plan](file:///C:/Users/voothi/.gemini/antigravity-ide/brain/4aeda6c0-19d2-44d2-9cce-2a9bc9956b4d/implementation_plan.md)** which outlines the exact architectural fixes to: - Suppress the secondary subtitle in `drum_osd` whenever the tooltip is active. - Redirect the tooltip's vertical position to the secondary subtitle OSD region (top of the screen) during Drum Mode to prevent all overlap. Please review the plan and let me know if you approve so I can proceed to the execution phase.
