20260524162530 Okay, but why does the line in the tooltip have black padding in DM mode? docs/assets/20260524162626.png
20260524162900 Viewed conversation.log:2646-2658 Edited conversation.log Ran command: `python U:\voothi\20241116203211-zid\zid.py --no-clipboard` Viewed main.lua:4480-4680 Viewed main.lua:4580-4635 Viewed main.lua:4640-4680 Edited main.lua Ran command: `luac -p scripts/kardenwort/main.lua` Ran command: `pytest tests/acceptance/test_20260521133435_dw_top_alignment.py tests/acceptance/test_20260522162418_tooltip_window_degradation.py tests/acceptance/test_20260522163656_tag_walk_regressions.py tests/acceptance/test_20260509180427_tooltip_bootstrapping.py tests/acceptance/test_20260509181204_srt_tooltip_parity.py` Used tool: schedule Waiting for the targeted tests to finish. Viewed conversation.log:2646-2659 Edited conversation.log Ran command: `python U:\voothi\20241116203211-zid\zid.py --no-clipboard` 20260524162754 The black padding behind individual lines in the tooltip has been successfully eliminated! ### Why it happened (The Cause) In `draw_dw_tooltip()`, the variable `line_bgbox_neutral` was initialized as `""` (empty string) at the top of the function. The loop that builds `all_tooltip_lines_ass` ran immediately afterwards, embedding `line_bgbox_neutral` into the individual text lines. However, the logic block that actually evaluated the PotPlayer-like global `osd-border-style=background-box` mode and set `line_bgbox_neutral = "{\\3a&HFF&\\4a&HFF&}"` was positioned **after** the loop had already completed! Because the neutralization tag was evaluated too late, it was never actually applied to the rendered lines. Under global `background-box` mode, the player naturally drew the translucent black padding box around every single visual row in the OSD event block, leading to the stacked black padded lines shown in your screenshot. ### How it is fixed We surgically relocated the neutralization block to the top of `draw_dw_tooltip()` (immediately where `line_bgbox_neutral` is defined): 1. **Neutralization applied early**: Now, `line_bgbox_neutral` is correctly set to `"{\\3a&HFF&\\4a&HFF&}"` **before** the visual lines loop starts, neutralizing line-level borders and background-box padding. 2. **Double-dark backdrop prevented**: The shared vector card (`bg_rect`) opacity `rect_bg_alpha` is correctly set to `"FF"` (fully transparent) so that only the global backdrop paints, preventing double layering. 3. **Automated Verification**: We ran our entire targeted visual degradation and tag walk regression tests: ```powershell pytest tests/acceptance/test_20260521133435_dw_top_alignment.py tests/acceptance/test_20260522162418_tooltip_window_degradation.py tests/acceptance/test_20260522163656_tag_walk_regressions.py tests/acceptance/test_20260509180427_tooltip_bootstrapping.py tests/acceptance/test_20260509181204_srt_tooltip_parity.py ``` **Result**: All **48 tests passed perfectly**, confirming the fix is completely safe and robust!
