20260524170128 # Resolve Drum Window Font Discrepancy & Restore Volume OSD (Dynamic Suspension) This plan outlines the design to enforce a premium voluminous outline and shadow style on kardenwort's Drum Window (DW) to perfectly match Drum Mode (DM), while seamlessly restoring the player's native OSD (like the volume bar and gray OSD text) by dynamically suspending the border style override during volume or mute events. ## User Review Required > [!IMPORTANT] > The dynamic OSD style override (`outline-and-shadow`) is preserved when kardenwort is active to ensure the custom vector panels render with high-end, premium outlines and shadows. > To prevent any native OSD regressions (like the volume bar disappearing or gray text looking strange), we introduce a smart **Dynamic Volume Suspension** mechanism that temporarily restores the player's native `background-box` style for 2 seconds whenever a volume or mute event occurs. > We also style the DW text lines and card with the exact premium border/shadow configurations from DM, eliminating the flat font look. ## Proposed Changes --### Core Script #### [MODIFY] [main.lua](file:///u:/voothi/20260308110646-kardenwort-mpv/scripts/kardenwort/main.lua) 1. **Unify Primary Color Formatting**: - In `draw_dw` (around line 4377), change `\c&H%s&` to standard `\1c&H%s&` in `line_prefix` string formatting. 2. **Style DW Text Lines with Outlines & Shadows**: - Locate the `line_style` formatting inside `draw_dw` (around line 4433) and update it to apply the actual `Options.dw_border_size` and `Options.dw_shadow_offset` outlines/shadows: ```lua local line_style = string.format("{\\pos(960, %g)}{\\an8}{\\bord%g}{\\shad%g}{\\3c&H%s&}{\\4c&H%s&}{\\3a&H%s&}{\\4a&H%s&}{\\q2}", vl_y_top, Options.dw_border_size, Options.dw_shadow_offset, Options.dw_bg_color, Options.dw_bg_color, bg_alpha, bg_alpha) ``` 3. **Style DW Vector Background Card with Outlines & Shadows**: - Update `bg_rect` formatting inside `draw_dw` (around line 4452) to also apply custom outlines/shadows, giving the background window a beautifully voluminous and premium border frame: ```lua local bg_rect = string.format("{\\pos(%g, %g)}{\\an7}{\\bord%g}{\\shad%g}{\\3c&H%s&}{\\4c&H%s&}{\\3a&H%s&}{\\4a&H%s&}{\\1c&H%s&}{\\1a&H%s&}{\\p1}m 0 0 l %g 0 l %g %g l 0 %g{\\p0}", rect_left, rect_top, Options.dw_border_size, Options.dw_shadow_offset, Options.dw_bg_color, Options.dw_bg_color, bg_alpha, bg_alpha, Options.dw_bg_color, bg_alpha, rect_w, rect_w, rect_h, rect_h) ``` 4. **Enhance UI Border Override with Dynamic Volume Suspension**: - Locate the function `manage_ui_border_override(enable)` (around line 8494) and implement dynamic volume/mute OSD suspension logic: ```lua local volume_suspension_timer = nil local function apply_border_override_state() if FSM.volume_suspension_active then -Temporarily restore native style local saved = FSM.saved_osd_border_style if saved and saved ~= "" then local cur = mp.get_property("osd-border-style") if cur ~= saved then mp.set_property("osd-border-style", saved) FSM.osd_border_style = saved end end else -Apply the override to outline-and-shadow if (FSM.ui_border_override_depth or 0) > 0 then local cur = mp.get_property("osd-border-style") if cur == "background-box" then FSM.saved_osd_border_style = "background-box" mp.set_property("osd-border-style", "outline-and-shadow") FSM.osd_border_style = "outline-and-shadow" end else -Restore saved local saved = FSM.saved_osd_border_style if saved and saved ~= "" then local cur = mp.get_property("osd-border-style") if cur ~= saved then mp.set_property("osd-border-style", saved) FSM.osd_border_style = saved end end FSM.saved_osd_border_style = nil end end end function manage_ui_border_override(enable) if enable then FSM.ui_border_override_depth = (FSM.ui_border_override_depth or 0) + 1 if FSM.ui_border_override_depth > 1 then return end apply_border_override_state() else FSM.ui_border_override_depth = math.max(0, (FSM.ui_border_override_depth or 0) - 1) if FSM.ui_border_override_depth > 0 then return end apply_border_override_state() end end local function trigger_volume_suspension() if not FSM.saved_osd_border_style then return end FSM.volume_suspension_active = true apply_border_override_state() if volume_suspension_timer then volume_suspension_timer:kill() end volume_suspension_timer = mp.add_timeout(2.0, function() FSM.volume_suspension_active = false apply_border_override_state() end) end ``` 5. **Register Volume & Mute Observers**: - Register observers at the bottom of the observers block (around line 9485): ```lua mp.observe_property("volume", "number", trigger_volume_suspension) mp.observe_property("mute", "bool", trigger_volume_suspension) ``` ## Verification Plan ### Automated Tests We will execute the targeted pytest suites to ensure 100% of all 48 structural and behavior tests pass cleanly: ```powershell pytest tests/acceptance/test_20260521133435_dw_top_alignment.py tests/acceptance/test_20260522162418_tooltip_window_degradation.py tests/acceptance/test_20260522163656_tag_walk_regressions.py tests/acceptance/test_20260509180427_tooltip_bootstrapping.py tests/acceptance/test_20260509181204_srt_tooltip_parity.py ``` We will also verify syntax correctness using: ```powershell luac -p scripts/kardenwort/main.lua ``` ### Manual Verification The user can verify that: 1. The font and ASS rendering styles in Drum Window (DW) perfectly match Drum Mode (DM), appearing beautiful, outlined, and voluminous. 2. The player's native volume bar and gray OSD text appear natively and beautifully without layout issues whenever the volume is adjusted or muted.
