20260525041207 Why for low-resolution videos (144p) with long subtitles with hyphens in DW mode does not highlighting by dragging the first line from top to top or the last line down or by passing motion work? docs/assets/20260525041202.png
20260525041710 The reason was DW edge-scroll geometry, not the hyphens themselves. What happened: - In 144p / dense long subtitles, DW wraps many subtitles into multiple visual lines. - The total DW block can overflow the 1080 OSD frame. - Our DW auto-scroll trigger used the first/last hit-zone bounds. - When the first hit-zone is above the screen or the last hit-zone is below the screen, the trigger becomes unreachable. - So dragging from the top line upward, the last line downward, or through motion could stop selecting/scrolling because the mouse could never cross the calculated boundary. Fixed: - [main.lua](U:/voothi/20260308110646-kardenwort-mpv/scripts/kardenwort/main.lua): DW now detects when the visible text block overflows the top/bottom edge. - In overflow cases, DW uses the reachable screen edge zone again. - In normal non-overflow cases, the previous anti-spontaneous-scroll protection stays intact. Tests added: - [test_dw_pure_logic.py](U:/voothi/20260308110646-kardenwort-mpv/tests/unit/test_dw_pure_logic.py): added top/bottom overflow edge-scroll cases. - [test_20260522163656_tag_walk_regressions.py](U:/voothi/20260308110646-kardenwort-mpv/tests/acceptance/test_20260522163656_tag_walk_regressions.py): added structural guard so DW overflow keeps reachable triggers. Verified: ```powershell luac -p scripts\kardenwort\main.lua python -m pytest tests\unit\test_dw_pure_logic.py tests\acceptance\test_20260522163656_tag_walk_regressions.py ``` Result: `75 passed`.
