20260525125845 You were right: `tooltip_*_bg_opacity=100` was not a normal user-facing approach. It worked mechanically, but the naming was misleading because this code interprets numeric `0..100` as transparency, not opacity. I changed the solution to use preferred ASS alpha options: - `tooltip_bg_alpha=60`: default card alpha - `tooltip_dw_bg_alpha=`: empty, DW inherits default - `tooltip_dm_bg_alpha=FF`: DM extra card is fully transparent - `tooltip_srt_bg_alpha=FF`: SRT extra card is fully transparent ASS alpha is explicit: - `00` = opaque - `FF` = fully transparent The old `tooltip_*_bg_opacity` options still exist as legacy fallbacks, so existing configs should not break. Changed: - [mpv.conf](U:/voothi/20260308110646-kardenwort-mpv/mpv.conf):274 - [main.lua](U:/voothi/20260308110646-kardenwort-mpv/scripts/kardenwort/main.lua):458 - Resolver logic in [main.lua](U:/voothi/20260308110646-kardenwort-mpv/scripts/kardenwort/main.lua):3138 - Trace note in [renderer-unification-notes.md](U:/voothi/20260308110646-kardenwort-mpv/openspec/changes/20260525114328-unify-dw-dm-tooltip-renderer/renderer-unification-notes.md):35 Checked: - `luac -p scripts/kardenwort/main.lua` - `pytest tests/acceptance/test_20260522163656_tag_walk_regressions.py -q`: `45 passed` I did not run the full test suite.
